+Get jobs for a function
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+To find the jobs that run a given function, use ``Scheduler.get_jobs_for()``.
+This avoids keeping ``Job`` objects around just to cancel them later.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import schedule
+
+    def hello():
+        print('Hello world')
+
+    scheduler = schedule.Scheduler()
+    scheduler.every().second.do(hello)
+
+    for job in scheduler.get_jobs_for(hello):
+        scheduler.cancel_job(job)
+
+
+Pause and resume jobs
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+To temporarily stop all jobs with a tag, use ``schedule.pause(tag)``.
+Paused jobs are skipped by ``run_pending()`` until ``schedule.resume(tag)``
+is called. Jobs stay registered, so there is no need to re-add them.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import schedule
+
+    schedule.every().hour.do(backup).tag('db')
+
+    schedule.pause('db')   # maintenance window
+    schedule.resume('db')
+
+
 Cancel all jobs
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 To remove all jobs from the scheduler, use ``schedule.clear()``
